The complement of Exists: Missing returns the os.Stat error only inside the
errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist) branch. The syscall.Errno / errno sentinels may match
through Errno.Is, so they must be kept (under *fs.PathError.Unwrap, no fmt.Errorf);
dropping them all would be wrong, as would adding a sentinel fs.ErrNotExist origin.
-fanout 0 keeps the entries ungrouped so that chains and guard marks are visible.
-- args --
-fanout 0 source/source.go:@missing
